Subject: [PATCH 3/3] K636: find the report collections on Windows

Reports 5, 6 and 8 are declared in separate top-level collections of
interface 1. Linux (hidraw) reaches all of them through one path; Windows
gives each collection its own path (&col05, &col06, &col08), and a report
can only be sent through the collection that declares it.

The detector now reads each vendor collection's report descriptor
(hid_get_report_descriptor; on Windows hidapi rebuilds it per collection),
picks the path that declares each report, and gives the controller one
handle per report. On Linux all three are the same handle, so nothing
changes there.

All collections of one keyboard share one claim key (the path without
&colNN and its instance suffix), so the keyboard is probed once. A
keyboard whose collections are still arriving after being plugged in is
not remembered as rejected; only a failed model probe is. The location is
the command collection's path, so saved profiles match on every start.

Refs #5588
